t breaking the meld. Wait \u2014 correction: my hand contains W7, W8, W9? No \u2014 I have an exposed meld [W7, W8, W9], so those three are not in hand. My hand tiles are: [W1, W2, W3, W4, T3\u00d72, F2, J1] \u2014 total 8 distinct holdings? Wait, count: W1, W2, W3, W4, T3, T3, F2, J1 \u2192 8 tiles. But a hand should have 13 before drawing. Something\u2019s off.\n\nWait: standard hand size is 13 tiles before draw. After drawing, 14, then discard. But here, after melds, hand size adjusts.\n\nI have one meld (3 tiles), so hand should have 11 tiles to make 14. But listed hand: W1, W2, W3, W4, W7, W8, W9, T3\u00d72, F2, J1 \u2192 that's 11 tiles. But W7, W8, W9 are *already in the meld*, so why are they in hand?\n\nAh \u2014 **critical clarification**: In standard notation, once a meld is exposed (via Chi/Peng/Gang), those three tiles are moved from hand to the front. So they should not appear in \"hand tiles\".\n\nBut here, \u201cYour hand tiles are\u201d includes W7, W8, W9 \u2014 which conflicts with having a meld [W7, W8, W9].\n\nTherefore, likely error in presentation: probably the hand tiles list includes *all* personal tiles, including those in melds? Unlikely.\n\nAlternative: perhaps \u201chand tiles\u201d means current concealed hand, and the meld is separate. So if I have a meld [W7, W8, W9], then W7, W8, W9 should not be in hand.\n\nBut in the list: \u201cYour hand tiles are: [W1: 1; W2: 1; W3: 1; W4: 1; W7: 1; W8: 1; W9: 1; T3: 2; F2: 1; J1: 1]\u201d \u2014 that\u2019s 10 tiles. Meld has 3 \u2192 total 13. But I should have 13 in hand before drawing, then 14, then discard.\n\nUnless I just drew \u2014 but no indication.\n\nWait \u2014 valid actions include \u201cPlay W7\u201d, \u201cPlay W8\u201d, etc. \u2014 meaning I can discard W7? That implies W7 is still in hand.\n\nThis suggests the meld [W7, W8, W9] was formed earlier, but somehow I still hold individual W7, W8, W9? Impossible.\n\nAh \u2014 realization: the game history shows \u201cChi W8\u201d \u201